               synth - general DBBC3 synthesizer communication

  Syntax:     synth=n,data_to

  Response:   synth/n,data_from


Settable parameters:
  n           Synthesizer number, 1-4
  data_to     Complete message to be sent to synthesizer; no checking is
              performed.

Monitor-only parameters:
  data_from   response of synthesizer, if any.

Comments:

IMPORTANT: The 'data_to' parameter should NOT include the string 'rst' (case
insensitive). That string will cause the device to lose its factory
calibration.

This command sends a low-level communication message to a synthesizer and
presents the response. The response may span multiple lines corresponding to
the lines sent by the synthesizer. All lines except the final one will be
labeled as '#dbbcn#dbbc3/' without the synthesizer number. The final response
line will include the synthesizer prompt.

Communication with the synthesizer is accomplished through the DBBC3. The user
should not put 'synth=n,' at the start of the 'data_to' field as the command
will do this automatically. Multiple synthesizer commands can be included in
one 'data_to' by separating them with semicolons (';').

The 'synth' command cannot be used if the rack type in 'equip.ctl' specifies a
'dbbc' (DBBC2) type. Other rack types do not limit the use of this command.
